  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_SPECS` | `specs/README.md` absent, or no approved scope spec to scaffold |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Tasks exist + mode verb absent (per `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`) |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A rule reference or `<DependsOn>` entry does not resolve to an existing file (`AX_RULES_RESOLUTION_HARD_FAIL`) |
    | `H_RULES_CYCLE` | `<DependsOn>` closure cycles during per-phase rule activation (STEP_3) |
    | `H_VERIFICATION_COMMAND_MISSING` | A `<RequiresVerification>` alias is absent from infra-spec Verification Commands (alias, ticket ID) |
    | `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING` | The target scope being scaffolded (the intake target) lacks a Bootstrap Requirements section — checked ONLY for that scope, not for every ✅ scope in the Portal (did not pass the scope flow) |
    | `H_ID_COLLISION` | A generated Task-ID / slug collides with an existing one |
    | `H_TYPING_SCENARIO_MISSING` | A DbC contract in Spec References has no `contract`-level typing scenario mapped to a test |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the breakdown or the test plan |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Read the Portal; detect scopes, graph, mode. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Scope names, types, and statuses come from the current portal's Scope Graph + Scopes table
        (`sdd-state`, per `AX_SCOPE_GRAPH_DETECTION`) already in context — the skill that dispatched
        this flow already called it; a fresh `sdd-state` call here is a wasted turn. Read
        `specs/README.md` itself ONLY for the one thing that snapshot does not carry: the
        dependency edges A→B of the Mermaid Scope Graph (absent portal → `H_NO_SPECS`). Read each
        ✅ scope spec and its module specs — specs only, never code (`AX_SPEC_IS_SOLE_SOURCE`).
        Detect mode per `AX_DIRECTIVE_MODE` / `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`
        — **detection table (directive-specific):**

        | Mode | Detection |
        |---|---|
        | `initial` | No `*.3-tasks.md` exists yet anywhere under the target scope (module / scope index absent) |
        | `extend-dag` | A `*.3-tasks.md` index already exists for the target scope and intake adds tickets to it |
        | — ambiguous | Index(es) exist but intake states neither add-tickets nor any mode verb → `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` |

        `extend-dag` reads existing tickets and preserves their IDs
        (`AX_EXTEND_DAG_PRESERVES_EXISTING_IDS`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_0B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear the FLOW_VERSION/READINESS preflight gate before scaffolding.</Goal>
      <Action>
        `sdd-state` already reports `FLOW_VERSION` / `READINESS`. When `READINESS=not-ready`, run
        `sdd-task` (no Task-ID) for the map — its `гейты:` line, when present, names the queued
        TODO tickets already building the missing gate scripts; that is the fact the switch below
        checks, never a guess. Size the gate to this request's own blast radius
        (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`).

        {{> "contract/process/readiness-preflight-gate"}}
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CASCADE">
      <Goal>Resolve the rules cascade. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read the rule registry — `ai/directives/knowledge.xml`, `<Rules>` section. Per scope, resolve
        the effective rule-set per `AX_RULES_CASCADE_RESOLUTION`:
        1. collect the traversed-scopes tier — union of Effective Rules from every scope reachable via
           `depends-on` from the target scope (transitive closure);
        2. overlay the target-scope tier (scope spec Effective Rules for infra; Rules for
           product/library), then each `module:<name>` tier (module spec Handoff Module Rules
           Additions), then task-tier rules the operator supplied — later tier wins on collision;
        3. resolve every rule ref to an existing file (`AX_RULES_RESOLUTION_HARD_FAIL`, else
           `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`);
        4. build the per-scope Cascade Table (Scope × Categories) destined for
           `specs/<scope>/<scope>.3-tasks.md`.
        No operator stop — mechanical.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_DAG">
      <Goal>Build the acyclic task DAG. — GATE 1: operator approves the BREAKDOWN.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Bootstrap Requirements of the target scope's spec → Phase-0 bootstrap tickets
        (`AX_BOOTSTRAP_TICKET_DERIVATION`); missing section on the target scope →
        `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING` (checked only for the scope in intake, not for other
        ✅ scopes reachable via the graph). Form tickets per
        `AX_DAG_AND_TICKET_BOUNDARIES` (one per coherent spec unit; subdivide only for parallelism or
        context overflow); cross-scope placement per `AX_CROSS_SCOPE_TASK_PLACEMENT`; assign slugs
        (`AX_TASK_ID_UNIQUENESS`). Acyclic. **Present the DAG (the breakdown) as a decision card and
        get operator approval — this is the one gate on structure.** STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_TASK_GENERATION">
      <Goal>Generate tickets + test plan. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Create each new ticket from its STEP_2 DAG owner: module-owned →
        `npx gennady sdd-new task --scope <scope> --module <module> --id <ACR>-<slug>`; scope-owned →
        `npx gennady sdd-new task --scope <scope> --id <ACR>-<slug>` (omit `--module`, never invent one).
        Scope/module/ID come verbatim from that DAG node. The command never overwrites and
        prints the section manifest (which sections are REQUIRED and what to fill). Content guidance
        per `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/task-ticket-structure.xml")`. Per
        ticket: decompose into phases (`AX_PHASES_DECLARED_IN_HEADER`; impl and test always separate). Activate
        rules per phase (`AX_RULE_ACTIVATION_PLAN`):
        1. candidates = the scope's cascade set from STEP_1;
        2. include each candidate whose `<Triggers>` match THIS phase's `Target Files` + `kind` and
           whose `<SkipWhen>` does not apply;
        3. close the set over `<DependsOn>` transitively — open each included rule file, add every
           dependency, recurse until the set stops growing (cycle → `H_RULES_CYCLE`; missing file →
           `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`) — the list ships fully resolved, the phase-subagent never walks
           `<DependsOn>` at runtime;
        4. write the phase `Rules:` bullet list — one `[<rule-id>](<rule-file-path>)` per rule, direct
           + transitive, all explicit;
        4b. per `AX_BOOTSTRAP_TICKET_DERIVATION`'s shared-infra-file ownership rule: when this phase
            reads or extends a shared infra file (`package.json` scripts, `.nvmrc`, a tool config)
            owned by a DIFFERENT bootstrap ticket, write an explicit `владелец — <ticket>` line into
            this phase's text naming that owner — never leave it for the worker to reconstruct by
            grepping sibling tickets;
        5. after all phases: union `<RequiresVerification>` aliases across the ticket's phases, group
           rules by alias, resolve each unique alias from infra-spec Verification Commands (absent →
           `H_VERIFICATION_COMMAND_MISSING`), and write ticket Verification table — one row
           per unique alias, Required-by = comma-separated declaring rule IDs.
        Draft BDD with the mandatory `contract`-level
        typing scenario per contract (`AX_TICKET_HAS_BDD_AND_TESTS`) and, per `AX_E2E_FIRST`, an
        `e2e`-level scenario for the ticket's user-facing path by default — dropping it needs a
        named Decision Log entry with a risk line, not a quiet "unit is enough" call by the phase
        subagent; pre-fill the Execution Log plan
        (`AX_EXECUTION_LOG_PLAN_VS_FACT`). Error-path and edge-case scenarios are drafted NOW, at this
        step, not left for a later pass (`AX_RELEASE_READY_DEFAULT` — release-ready is the default
        depth unless the operator named POC/MVP); an error scenario asserts against the thrown error
        class + a stable message fragment (`AX_FOCUSED_ERROR_ASSERTIONS`), never a `Result` shape,
        since the canon public-API error mechanism is throw + try/catch (`AX_RESULT_PUBLIC_BOUNDARY` —
        Result is a narrow, contract-scoped exception, not the default). **BDD coverage pass — dispatch
        ONE isolated subagent** with a
        clean slice (module spec + contract anchors + requirements + draft BDD) asking «which negative /
        corner / trust-boundary / failure-mode scenarios are missing?»; merge approved ones — never
        defer one to "later" without an explicit operator decision and a Decision Log entry naming the
        risk (`AX_RELEASE_READY_DEFAULT`) — log the
        reviewed checklist in the ticket Decision Log (`AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`,
        `DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT`). Validate every contract has its typing scenario
        mapped to a test (else `H_TYPING_SCENARIO_MISSING`). Check each emitted ticket against
        `TASK_TICKET_STRUCTURE`: section anchors match the normative names exactly
        (`AX_TICKET_SECTION_NAMES_NORMATIVE`), and contract material is linked by spec anchor with zero
        copied contract text (`AX_SSOT_TRACEABILITY`) — write every Meta `Spec References:` entry and
        every phase `Spec Refs:` entry in the RESOLVABLE form `<path>#<anchor>`, where `<anchor>` is
        either a `SECTION_NAME` the spec file wraps in `<!--SECTION:NAME-->` markers, or the
        GitHub-style heading slug (lowercase, hyphen-separated) `sdd-extract` resolves directly — e.g.
        `../greeting/greeting.spec.md#module-contracts` for the `## Module Contracts` heading, or
        `../greeting/greeting.spec.md#MODULE_CONTRACTS` when that section carries an explicit anchor.
        An anchor that is neither — a bare prose reference, a heading paraphrase, a line number — fails
        `sdd-task --phase`'s downstream read at execution time; a link a worker or auditor cannot
        resolve with `sdd-extract <file>#<anchor>` verbatim is not a valid Spec Reference. No operator
        stop — automated.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_TEST_PLAN_REVIEW">
      <Goal>GATE 2: operator approves the TEST PLAN.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Present the test plan as a decision card: each BDD scenario as a use-case, tagged
        `[<ACRONYM>-REQ-N]`, traced up to the scope Vision / goal it protects, plus coverage (every
        contract has a typing scenario, every scenario maps to a test). The operator approves **what is
        tested, which use-cases are covered, and that this guarantees the vision** — the one gate on
        substance. Out-of-scope proposals the subagent surfaced are raised here. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Write the index hierarchy; hand off. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        For each `<module>.3-tasks.md` that does not exist yet, run `npx gennady sdd-new module-index --scope
        <scope> --module <module>` to lay down the skeleton (nested `--module foo/bar` per
        `AX_HIERARCHICAL_SPECS`); an existing file is filled in place, never re-scaffolded. Fill per
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-tasks-index.xml")` (Tracker, Slug
        Registry, intra-module DAG, shared content per `AX_TICKET_DEDUPLICATION`). Roll up the scope
        tracker the same way — `npx gennady sdd-new scope-index --scope <scope>` when `<scope>.3-tasks.md` is
        missing, then fill per
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/scope-tasks-index.xml")` — and roll up
        the project index the same way — `npx gennady sdd-new project-index` when `specs/3-tasks.md` is missing,
        then fill per
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/project-tasks-index.xml")`; never a
        manual `Write` of `specs/3-tasks.md` from scratch.
        Then run `npx gennady sdd-check --all .` (task-DAG: id-collisions · deps resolve · acyclic; tracker↔ticket sync;
        phase graph; exec-log) and resolve or consciously defer every finding per
        `AX_CLOSE_WITH_INTEGRITY_CHECK` — the scaffold mutation is done only once the task graph passes.
        `BDD_COVERAGE` (canonical case names exist in the declared test file) gates on the ticket's
        own Meta Status — the existence check runs only once that ticket is `[x] DONE`, never for a
        freshly-scaffolded `[ ] TODO` ticket (whose test files do not exist yet by design), so a clean
        `sdd-check --all .` right after this step is expected, not a sign the check is silently
        skipped. Fix only structural findings at this step (id collisions, unresolved deps, cycles,
        tracker drift, broken `](…spec.md)` links) — a BDD/test-existence finding here would mean a
        ticket was mis-marked DONE before its tests exist, a scaffold defect worth fixing on its own,
        not phase noise to suppress.
        These trackers and tickets are read by execute with no memory of this scaffolding run —
        every DAG edge, rule reference, and BDD scenario must already be in the file
        (`AX_STATELESS_ARTIFACT`). Emit a created-files summary with traceability links. Hand off to
        execute in the SAME session —
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/execute.directive.xml")` — no operator stop;
        isolation lives one level down, at the phase-worker subagent execute dispatches per phase, not
        at this handoff.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

